{
  "id": "ideal-observer",
  "term": "ideal observer",
  "definition": "An ideal observer is a model or computer algorithm that performs a specific perceptual task as well as mathematically possible given the information available and the limits built into the model. In psychology, it is used as a baseline for comparing human performance so researchers can judge how efficiently people use the information in a stimulus and how difficult the task itself is.",
